message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2143-01-06 22:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2143-01-06 22:35:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been really sick the past two days—nauseous, throwing up, and constant diarrhea. I couldn’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2143-01-06 22:36:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever, chills, or pain in your abdomen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2143-01-06 22:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever or chills. My stomach doesn’t hurt, but I feel weak and dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2143-01-06 22:38:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You’ve been on IV tigecycline for your left leg infection, right? That antibiotic can sometimes cause nausea and diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2143-01-06 22:39:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been on it for about six weeks. Could that really be causing this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2143-01-06 22:40:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. We’re going to pause the tigecycline for now and start you on oral vancomycin just in case it’s C. diff, but we suspect it’s a side effect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2143-01-06 22:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So you think stopping the antibiotic will help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2143-01-06 22:43:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ll switch you to a different IV antibiotic that’s less likely to cause stomach issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2143-01-07 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show your white count is elevated, but kidney function is stable. The diarrhea seems to be improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2143-01-07 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t vomited since last night, and the diarrhea is less frequent. That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2143-01-07 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’re going to start you on IV vancomycin and meropenem for your leg infection instead of tigecycline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2143-01-07 08:19:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is my leg infection getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2143-01-07 08:20:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s still concerning. The vascular surgery team will see you today to evaluate the wound."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The vascular surgeon examined your left stump. They cleaned out the wound, but the infection has gone deep into the bone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what does that mean? More antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Unfortunately, antibiotics alone won’t cure it. They recommend an above-knee amputation—AKA—to remove the infected bone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:04:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another amputation? I’m not sure I can handle that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:05:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But if we don’t remove the infected part, the infection could spread and become life-threatening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How soon would I need the surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:08:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They suggest scheduling it within the next two weeks. In the meantime, we’ll start you on Bactrim by mouth to help control the infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:09:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m allergic to Bactrim, isn’t that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:10:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see it’s listed in your allergies. We’ll avoid it and discuss alternatives with infectious disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:12:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just need some time to process this surgery decision."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2143-01-07 13:13:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. We’ll give you space and check back later. The team will support you through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2143-01-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We reviewed your urine test—there’s Klebsiella oxytoca, but it’s sensitive to several antibiotics, including meropenem, which you’re already on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2143-01-08 09:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I had the UTI symptoms before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2143-01-08 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly, but you’re not having symptoms now, so we’re covering it with your current antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2143-01-08 09:03:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my PICC line—was it checked?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2143-01-08 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the chest X-ray showed it was out of position, so it was repositioned yesterday. It’s now in the right spot near your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2143-01-08 09:06:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I felt discomfort in my chest?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2143-01-08 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. It should feel better now. We’ll monitor it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2143-01-08 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I spoke with infectious disease. Since you’re allergic to Bactrim, we’ll keep you on the IV antibiotics until surgery and adjust based on culture results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2143-01-08 15:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diabetes—has that been okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2143-01-08 15:02:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sugars have been stable on your usual insulin—Lantus and Humalog. No changes needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2143-01-08 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been worried about everything piling up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2143-01-08 15:05:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. You’ve been through a lot. But your nausea and diarrhea have resolved, your infection is being managed, and you’re making progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2143-01-09 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re discharging you today. Continue your insulin, and take the oral vancomycin for a few more days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2143-01-09 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2143-01-09 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call vascular surgery to schedule your AKA within the next two weeks. Keep taking your antibiotics and follow up with infectious disease for lab results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2143-01-09 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start feeling sick again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2143-01-09 10:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor or go to the ER if you have fever, increased pain, drainage from the wound, or blood in your stool."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2143-01-09 10:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’ll follow up on everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2143-01-09 10:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2143-01-06 22:34:00",
    "admission_end": "2143-01-09 19:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 58-year-old woman with type 1 diabetes and bilateral below-knee amputations was admitted for nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea while on a six-week course of IV tigecycline for presumed left stump osteomyelitis. Her gastrointestinal symptoms resolved after discontinuation of tigecycline, suggesting a medication side effect. She was transitioned to IV vancomycin and meropenem. Vascular surgery evaluated her left stump and recommended an above-knee amputation due to deep bone infection, which she agreed to schedule within two weeks. A urine culture grew Klebsiella oxytoca, sensitive to meropenem. Her PICC line was repositioned after imaging showed malposition. She remained stable, with controlled diabetes and improving infection markers, and was discharged home with plans for surgery and outpatient follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Diarrhea",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Chronic osteomyelitis, lower leg",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Infection (chronic) of amputation stump",
      "Tetracycline group causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Diabetes mellitus type 1",
      "Peripheral vascular disease, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
